Install a shared-guide pointer for one named agent, or use --all for every supported agent. Do not combine an agent with --all. Agents need not be installed.
--user is the default: Claude Code uses $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/skills or ~/.claude/skills, Antigravity ~/.gemini/config/skills, and all other agents ~/.agents/skills.
--project uses .claude/skills for Claude Code or .agents/skills for every other agent, under the exact cwd even outside Git. User overrides do not affect project paths. Each skill directory is named agent-cli.
The two scope flags are mutually exclusive. Current stubs are unchanged; older or edited owned stubs are updated. Foreign skills conflict unless --force replaces them. --dry-run writes nothing.
No hooks, settings changes or instruction-file edits. See skill show --pointer for other agents.

Usage: agent-cli skill install [agent]

Flags:
      --all      Select every supported agent (shared directories are handled once)
      --dry-run  Report planned actions without changing files
      --force    Replace a foreign skill at this build's skill path
      --project  Use the native agent skill path under the exact current directory
      --user     Use the agent's user skill location (default)
  -h, --help     Print help
  -v, --verbose  Print diagnostic details to stderr

Examples:
  agent-cli skill install codex
  agent-cli skill install claude --user
  agent-cli skill install antigravity --project --dry-run

Environment: CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR (Claude user scope only); system user home for --user
Exit codes: 0 installed, updated or unchanged · 1 filesystem failure or conflict · 2 usage error or unknown agent
